     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg a day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg a day under supervision. For OTC use the limit is 1,200 mg a day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. It may also be a typo, for example 1600 mg total daily or 400 mg four times daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose with the prescribing clinician. Typical adult regimens are:\n- 400 mg by mouth every 6 hours (1,600 mg a day)\n- 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2,400 mg a day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg a day)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg a day, the maximum)\n\nOrders also normally come from a licensed prescriber. If a clinician confirms a dose, or you send me the corrected order, I can enter it right away. If you want to go ahead with the original dose anyway, I'd need the prescriber to confirm it and document the reason."
      }
     ],
